  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Madagascar faces multiple climate hazards including tropical cyclones, droughts, and floods. The WMO Global GBON gap analysis (June 2023) identified significant limitations in the countrys observational network that require urgent intervention. Currently, the General Directorate of Meteorology (DGM) operates 20 synoptic surface observation stations, while ASECNA manages 4 GBON-compliant surface stations and 2 upper-air stations. To achieve full GBON compliance, Madagascar must upgrade 9 existin</narrative>
  </description>
